SOUNDDVR driver TIMER-ISR sequencer body (FUN_0000_03dd) recovered + the note-timing family
(0419 note-advance / 0415 release tail / 0579 device far-vector) faithfully segment-rebased.

Recovered via the 0x3dd re-decompile seed (approved driver-class: added 0x3dd to the snd
FIST_DRIVER_SEED_OFFS -> fist_snd.c rebaselines 9b642483 -> e6d610c5, reproducible; the 3 hard-pristine
engine md5s 61453e42/0051cb56/75c6d726 UNCHANGED).  Ghidra had decompiled the 0x3d6 far-jmp placeholder
as the empty app_entry_0000_03d6; the real ISR body is at 0x3dd.

asm-verified vs re_out/fist_snd_image.bin.  The whole family runs with TWO segments that Ghidra
scrambled (some accesses based at 0, some at engine-DGROUP 0x1c000, some at the bogus SS=0x2ba9 context):
  - DS = CS = the driver LOAD segment (fist_snd_base): the per-voice static state at cs:0x5e (current
    note word), cs:0x5f (current channel), cs:0x60+bx (active-note-per-voice, 0xff=free), cs:0x67+bx
    (alloc flag), cs:0x68+bx (duration counter), cs:0x6f+bx (note tag), cs:0x70+bx (note index).
  - SS = DGROUP (0x1c00): the arm gate word [ss:0x23e] (the sequencer runs its 7-voice scan only while
    ==2) and the DEVICE OBJECT at DGROUP:0x4fa (dev seg) / 0x4fc (status) / 0x4fe (note-descriptor-table
    OFFSET).  The note table VT = DGROUP:[word 0x4fe] is indexed by note*4 (flags byte at +2: 0x60/0x20
    key bits, 0x40 sustain, 0x10 mode, bit7 gate; 0x579 vs 0415 chosen by bit7&0x10).

FUN_0000_03dd (asm 0x3dd): reentrancy/arm guard [ss:0x23e]==2, then scan cs:0x60..0x66 for active voices
  and call the per-tick note-advance 0419(al=0xff, ah=ror(voice,1)) for each; decrement the arm counter
  while any voice is active, else chain (app_entry = the 0x3d6 ljmp-to-old-handler; the shim owns INT-8
  so the chain is a no-op here).  Ghidra mis-modeled the `push bx; push cs; call 0419; ...; pop bx` as
  `iVar4 = unaff_CS` (would clobber the loop counter) -> the asm restores bx via pop, dropped.

FUN_0000_0419 (asm 0x419): the note-advance/release worker (find-or-alloc voice slot, set the VT flags,
  dispatch 0415/0579, post the SMC voice binding via 1d62/1e13).  Store-width fix: `mov [0x5e],ax` is
  16-bit (Ghidra emitted a 32-bit store that would clobber cs:0x60/0x61).

FUN_0000_0415 (asm 0x4ac): the shared release/duration-decrement tail (xchg the active slot, dec the
  duration, clear VT bit 0x40 on expiry).

FUN_0000_0579 (asm 0x579): `lcall [ss:0xec]` = the device method far-vector at DGROUP:0xec.

Reached only under FIST_SB (the driver sound path is populated only by the FIST_SB-gated config/section
installs) + driven per-tick by the shim's INT-8 pump (fist_snd_isr_tick) -> the 26 video flows stay
byte-identical.

